              "teach": "This is the named trap, and the second command is the sting: <code>spec.storageClassName</code> is immutable once set, and a JSON patch that touches it is rejected outright — <code>Forbidden: spec is immutable after creation except resources.requests and volumeAttributesClassName for bound claims</code>. A strategic-merge patch setting the same empty string would report <code>patched (no change)</code> instead, because an empty string is a no-op against the merge — it proves nothing. Either way the fix is the same: delete the claim and create it again with the field written out. The <code>WaitForFirstConsumer</code> event is a second false trail — it suggests the claim is merely waiting for the Deployment, when in fact it is now in the wrong class and will never look at your volume."
