    "closing": "One Pod is one shared fate. Containers in the same Pod can see the same file only because the Pod owns the volume and lends it to each of them, which is why three kubectl run invocations can never solve this and why the same mountPath on three different volumes is not sharing at all. Use emptyDir: it is scoped to the Pod, it needs no node privileges, and hostPath is banned precisely because it escapes that scope. NODE_NAME comes from the downward API — fieldRef on spec.nodeName — because the scheduler, not you, decides the answer, and it decides it again on every recreate. Both long-lived containers must never exit: restartPolicy defaults to Always, so a container that finishes successfully is restarted and ends in CrashLoopBackOff with a BackOff event. Give the writer an append loop, not a single write, and give the reader tail -F so it survives a file that does not exist yet. Finally, gamma must do the reading itself: kubectl exec proves the mount and earns nothing, because the grader reads gamma stdout. See \"Expose Pod Information to Containers Through Environment Variables\" at kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/inject-data-application/environment-variable-expose-pod-information/ and \"emptyDir\" at kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/storage/volumes/#emptydir."
